 :the-loop-said-this-and-said-it-wrong
 "`:what-the-judge-cannot-see` has carried, since iteration-02: *THE TRAFFIC.
  Twelve consecutive reads of /_diag/hydrate returned sampled:false -- twelve
  isolates, none of which had ever hydrated. This loop prices a served read on a
  graph that currently serves none.*

  Both sentences are true and the conclusion drawn from them was wrong. `No
  isolate has hydrated THIS graph` was read as `there is no traffic`. The
  traffic exists. It is on a different graph, and nothing asked which graph the
  isolates that HAD hydrated were holding."

 :why-the-traffic-is-there
 "The 2026-08-10 routing change (`graph/for-request`): an s3 request for a
  bucket goes to `s3-bucket/<bucket>`, its own chain, because two clients
  writing anywhere on the shared graph serialise against each other. Real s3
  traffic therefore left the shared graph that day. What stayed behind is the
  526-document collection the shared graph accumulated before the split -- 87.5%
  of its seed by bytes, and the entire basis of h6 and most of h7's value."

 :what-this-changes
 {:h6 "Retracting the 91 inline-body documents was already down to $2.14 after
       the pinned decomposition. Those documents are on the graph with no
       readers, so in practice it is worth less than that -- irreversible
       deletion of production data to speed up reads nobody makes."
  :h7 "Its value is dominated by not parsing that same 526-document collection.
       On the traffic graph, which has 33 blocks rather than 84, the collection
       is not there at all."
  :h1 "Unaffected in principle -- phase A is phase A -- but its SIZE is a
       property of the graph, and the traffic graph is 2.5x smaller by block
       count."
  :the-baseline "class-b-ops 84 and 11,462,579 bytes describe the wrong graph."}

 :what-is-not-invalidated
 "The method, the instruments, and the structural findings. A query is still 1%
  of a request. The harness still has to build from pins. The cold-isolate rate
  is still 6 in 10. Those are properties of the code path, not of which graph it
  walks."

 :the-shape-again
 "Fourth instance in one session of a measurement that cannot name its inputs --
  and this one names the SUBJECT rather than an input. A scaling constant whose
  calibration decayed; a premise inferred from a counter answering a different
  question; a build input with no revision in it; and now a graph nobody
  checked, priced for eight iterations, chosen because it was the graph that
  happened to be under the first probe."

 ;; ── CORRECTION, same day, 3 minutes later ──────────────────────────────────
 :correction
 {:at "2026-08-18T11:01Z"
  :what-was-claimed
  "That every observed hydrate is `s3-bucket/cloud-itonami-kouhou`, and by
   implication that kotobase-protocols-v2 has no readers."
  :what-happened
  "A sampler left running past the window recorded, within three minutes:

     10:58   s3-bucket/cloud-itonami-kouhou only
     10:59   kotobase-protocols-v2 at 10:59:25 and 10:59:29
     11:01   kotobase-protocols-v2 at 10:59:10, :19, :25, :29 -- four hydrates
             in 19 seconds -- and a THIRD graph, s3-bucket/4054fd3a10f226c2"

  :so-the-window-claim-stands-and-the-generalisation-does-not
  "`Of 34 hydrated isolates observed 10:36-10:58Z, all 34 held
   s3-bucket/cloud-itonami-kouhou` is what was measured and it remains true.
   `kotobase-protocols-v2 has no readers` was an inference from it, and it is
   false: that graph took four hydrates in 19 seconds at 10:59.

   Traffic on this Worker is BURSTY and multi-graph. A 22-minute window sees
   one graph; the next three minutes see three. The original finding was itself
   produced by looking at a longer window than the one that produced the
   error it corrected, and it was still too short."

  :and-the-limit-that-cannot-be-measured-from-here
  "Whose traffic. This workstation runs many concurrent agent sessions against
   the same production hosts, and a hydrate recorded by an isolate carries no
   caller identity. The 10:59 burst on kotobase-protocols-v2 was not driven by
   this session -- every request it made after 10:57:45 was a BARE diagnostic
   read, which does not hydrate -- but `not mine` is not `a user`. Agent
   traffic and organic traffic are indistinguishable from this vantage point,
   and every traffic statement in this loop inherits that."

  :what-survives-of-the-finding
  "The routing fact, which is not a traffic observation: since 2026-08-10 an s3
   request for a bucket goes to its own chain, so the 526-document collection
   on the shared graph is reachable there only by the four credential-gated
   query surfaces. That is read from `graph/for-request`, not from a sample,
   and it is what makes h6 and much of h7 worth less than their numbers say.

   What does NOT survive is `no readers`. Per-graph unit economics still need
   per-graph measurement, and the traffic mix needs a window measured in hours,
   not minutes."}

 :next
 "Re-measure per graph -- `s3-bucket/cloud-itonami-kouhou` at 33 blocks and
